WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:01.767
-Jack Whitehall!

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.434
Jack,
it's great to see you again.

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:05.434
-It's lovely to be here.
-Welcome back.

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:06.934
I know -- You have stories.

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:08.100
I want to ask you about this,

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.667
'cause you just came back
from the Super Bowl.

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:11.434
-Oh, my God, yeah.
The Super Bowl.

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:14.300
-Now, yes, that's a --
Now, do you know what that is?

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.400
-Yes. I am now --
I was under the impression

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.801
that I was attending
a Rihanna concert, but...

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:20.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:22.300
yes, some football
did break out sporadically.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.100
I've got to say,
as well, Philly fans --

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.734
they can put their alcohol away.

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:26.934
-Oh, yeah, yeah.
-Oh, my God!

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:28.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
-They know how to do it.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.501
-I've never seen anything
like it.

00:00:29.501 --> 00:00:30.634
10:00 in the morning.

00:00:30.634 --> 00:00:31.767
I was like,
"I'll go there early.

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:33.133
I'll soak up some of
the atmosphere."

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.834
There was a Philly fan in
a jersey and the face paint,

00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:38.868
big tall boy of lager,
peeing up against a wall.

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:41.701
Going, "Fly, Eagles, fly!"

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:43.367
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:46.334
And I have to say,
the men weren't much better.

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:47.868
It was...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.868 --> 00:00:49.834
-I didn't know that.
Oh, my goodness.

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:52.601
Peeing against the wall.

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:54.267
But it must have been --
Is it different --

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:56.367
I mean, there's nothing like
that quite in England, is there?

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:58.634
-No. I mean, like, the scale of
it compared to, like,

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:00.534
sport in the U.K. --
like, sport is a joke.

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:04.067
Like, the halftime show.
Oh, my God. Rihanna -- amazing.

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:06.300
In England, when you watch,
like, the Premier League,

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.801
our halftime shows,
they just put on, like,

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:11.701
Neil Diamond's "Sweet Caroline,"
and send out the mascot.

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:14.133
And you have Rihanna doing,
like, a full-blown concert

00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:17.400
with hundreds of dancers
and fireworks and a light show.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.000
Ours is a couple of
local kindergarten kids

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.334
kicking penalties past a
grown man dressed as a dinosaur.

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.100
-Yeah. That sounds
pretty good, actually.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.167
-Yeah, I know.
-I like that. Not bad.

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:29.968
Yesterday was Valentine's Day.

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:32.534
And did you get a chance to
celebrate with your girlfriend?

00:01:32.534 --> 00:01:35.601
-Oh, I'm afraid I'm on tour over
here, she's back in England,

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:38.334
so it was spent alone
in my hotel room

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:40.534
eating Popeyes chicken and
watching a couple episodes of

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:41.667
"Naked and Afraid."

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.701
-Oh, my gosh!

00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:46.901
Are you a romantic guy?

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:49.033
-Yeah, I mean,
I'm quite a romantic person.

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:51.100
She sent me gifts, as well.
-Oh, she did?

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.634
-Yeah. But she doesn't --
She just buys me

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.534
passive-aggressive presents now.

00:01:54.534 --> 00:01:56.033
So, like, it was just,
like, a load of

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.501
toiletries
and cleaning products,

00:01:57.501 --> 00:02:00.734
'cause she thinks that
I won't wash when I'm on tour.

00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:02.634
And she, like,
has a habit of doing this.

00:02:02.634 --> 00:02:04.200
She did it, actually, Christmas.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.701
She bought me something
called the Manscaper.

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:10.200
Are you aware of -- Do you --
Are you a manscaper yourself?

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.767
-That's -- I'm way past that.
No, I don't.

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:15.501
-What? That surprises me.

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:16.868
I look at you
and I would be like,

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:19.634
"This guy is like a dolphin
from the neck down."

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:22.767
You look so smooth.

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:26.067
You must manscape.
-In some ways, I am.

00:02:28.834 --> 00:02:30.567
-Yes, I walked in on you
in your dressing room,

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:31.834
and that's a blowhole.

00:02:34.567 --> 00:02:36.200
-That's what it is.
-Row that back in to shore.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.300
-That's right, yeah.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.467
-Yeah, but, so,
I use the Manscaper

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:40.400
'cause I, previously,
was like, you know,

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:41.801
Chewbacca from the neck down.

00:02:41.801 --> 00:02:43.634
And I was like --
Well, my girlfriend gave me

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:45.334
this Manscaper --
passive-aggressive present.

00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:46.367
-That's nice.
That's nice of her.

00:02:46.367 --> 00:02:47.434
-"Deal with yourself."

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:50.133
So, anyway, I started u-- Sorry.

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:51.767
I'm going into
quite a lot of detail here.

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:53.300
Sorry to put anyone off
their dinner plans.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:56.133
But I started keeping myself
a little bit tidy.

00:02:56.133 --> 00:02:57.601
I had this
awful situation, though,

00:02:57.601 --> 00:02:59.000
because I was using
the Manscaper

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.100
and I looked down
and I saw a red hair.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:02.300
And I was like, "Oh, my God.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.334
Maybe I'm going
ginger down there."

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:07.767
I Googled it.
Not, like, a thing.

00:03:07.767 --> 00:03:11.667
So then I was like, "Oh, my God.
Well, then whose hair is it?

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:15.167
Another man has been
scaping in my bathroom!"

00:03:15.167 --> 00:03:16.601
And she came back from the show.

00:03:16.601 --> 00:03:18.434
I confronted her,
holding aloft this hair.

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:19.968
I was like, "Who is he?
Where is he?"

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:22.534
And she came clean.
She was laughing in my face.

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:24.000
Do you know how it got there?

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:28.734
She admitted that she had been
using my Manscaper on the dog.

00:03:28.734 --> 00:03:30.734
[ Applause ]

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:35.901
-Well, there you go.
-Unacceptable.

00:03:35.901 --> 00:03:37.267
-But the dog looks great.

00:03:37.267 --> 00:03:38.601
-Oh, yeah, the dog --
Coco looks --

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:39.868
Lovely little Brazilian she did.

00:03:39.868 --> 00:03:42.000
It's a lovely...
-Yeah.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.701
Right now, you're on tour
all across North America.

00:03:44.701 --> 00:03:46.534
Look, you're in Philly
February 16th --

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:48.901
tomorrow, you're in Philly,
at The Miller Theater.

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:50.100
Then you're back here
this Friday

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.300
at the Beacon Theatre
in New York.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:52.400
-Yeah.
-That's fun -- in New York.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.334
-I'm so excited.
-Do you...

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:57.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:03:57.501 --> 00:04:01.167
-Do you remember
your first gig in America?

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:03.434
-I do. It was -- Yes.

00:04:03.434 --> 00:04:08.000
It was not as prestigious as
the Beacon Theatre in New York.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.701
It was actually just after
I'd done my U.K. tour,

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:12.834
and I'd finished
at Wembley Stadium

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:14.801
and had this amazing experience.

00:04:14.801 --> 00:04:17.067
It was so cool.
And I flew over to L.A.

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:19.167
And I said to my agent, "Yeah,
just book me a gig so that,

00:04:19.167 --> 00:04:20.634
you know,
I don't get too rusty."

00:04:20.634 --> 00:04:22.934
And he sent me
the address of the gig.

00:04:22.934 --> 00:04:24.968
And I arrived at the address

00:04:24.968 --> 00:04:28.167
and I looked up,
and it was a sex shop.

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:31.167
And I was like, "Oh, this must
be some kind of a joke."

00:04:31.167 --> 00:04:33.200
I walked in. I looked around.
I called my agent.

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:34.501
I was like, "Ha-ha, very funny.

00:04:34.501 --> 00:04:36.334
You've sent me the address
for a sex shop."

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:38.934
And he went,
"No, that's where the gig is.

00:04:38.934 --> 00:04:41.000
It's like a
quirky alternative night.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:44.200
They just put out some chairs,
and the show is in a sex shop."

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.100
And I said, "Well, I'm sorry.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.734
I do have some standards,
and this does not meet

00:04:48.734 --> 00:04:50.701
the threshold for what
I'm willing --

00:04:50.701 --> 00:04:52.767
I'm not performing in
a sex shop."

00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:54.133
And I hung up.

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:55.567
I said, "Just, you know,
make an excuse,

00:04:55.567 --> 00:04:57.467
say that I'm delayed, or my
plane crashed into the ocean.

00:04:57.467 --> 00:04:58.534
I don't care.

00:04:58.534 --> 00:04:59.801
I'm not doing a show in
a sex shop."

00:04:59.801 --> 00:05:01.133
-Yes.

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:03.200
-And then the bloody owner
of the gig comes over.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.534
He's like,
"Are you here for the comedy?"

00:05:04.534 --> 00:05:06.767
And I was like, "No,"

00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:09.133
and then realized,
because I'd said "no,"

00:05:09.133 --> 00:05:11.434
that I would have to act like
I was just a customer

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:13.534
in the sex shop.

00:05:13.534 --> 00:05:17.067
So, I was, like, browsing
through some of the items,

00:05:17.067 --> 00:05:18.901
trying on a couple of
nipple tassels.

00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:21.434
-Oh, my God!
-I walked straight out of there.

00:05:21.434 --> 00:05:24.434
I was like, "This is
too humiliating even for me."

00:05:24.434 --> 00:05:27.200
So I'm so pleased that,
on this tour, as you can see,

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:29.267
there's not a single sex shop.

00:05:29.267 --> 00:05:31.033
-But he is available.

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:33.634
He's available for bookings at
sex shops, if you really want.

00:05:33.634 --> 00:05:35.534
He's the one-and-only
Jack Whitehall, everybody.

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:36.834
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:36.834 --> 00:05:41.934
-For more info on Jack's tour,
go to jackwhitehall.com.

00:05:41.934 --> 00:05:45.167
Always great to see you, buddy.
-You are hairier than I thought.

00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:46.234
-More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:05:46.234 --> 00:05:47.300
Stick around, everybody.

